e she  was going to kill her own sister but in  season seven we did see Arya change her  mind and decide to go home instead of  going to King's Landing to try and kill  the Queen Cersei Lannister  aurilla did have an opportunity to go to  King's Landing and we know she had a bag  of faces with her but when she found out  Jon took Winterfell back from the  Bolton's she did decide to go home and  be with her family Arya and Sansa nearly  killed each other but they did make up  at the end and now John is on his way  home - and I know Arya is going to be  very excited to see John when it comes  to the stark siblings I think no one has  a stronger bond than John and Arya do  they are truly brother and sister no  matter who John's parents really are but  the reunion will be short-lived because  the night king is coming and this will  leave little time for the Starks to sit  down and enjoy each other's company I  don't think we will be seeing Oriole Eve  anytime soon - go finish off her list  not with what's coming from the north I  think the first thing Arya will do is  play her part in this war that's to come  all of us already know Arya is an  absolute badass and now she has a  Valyrian steel dagger which is exactly  what's needed to kill the others John  will probably want to keep his family  members safe though I don't think John  will want Arya out there on the  battlefield but I don't think he's gonna  have much of a choice  I think Arya will refuse to sit on the  sidelines while everyone else is  fighting Plus John has already said he  needs every man woman and child out  there helping win this war I believe we  will CRE out there fighting alongside  John and his other men  and not only will Oriya help but I also  believe she will kill at least one white  Walker if not more depending on how many  are actually left she has a Valyrian  steel dagger for a reason and it will be  put to good use but assuming Oriya  survives this great war what would she  do next if Jaime Lannister ends up  killing Cersei in the Hound ends up  killing his brother that would leave  nothing else for Arya to do in terms of  her story the show will be ending soon  and we may never actually see what Arya  does next but I think it's fun to  imagine these things anyway after all  the wars are over and everyone on arias  hit list is dead I think there are a few  different options I could see for arias  story moving forward the first one I  want to talk about is what we saw when  Arya reunited what there direwolf  Nymeria I know some people believe we  will see Nymeria again but there is a  chance we may not and if that's the case  then arias story may end in a similar  fashion to how my marry has ended  Arya tried to get Nymeria  come with her but then she realized she  never would because that's not in her  nature now Nymeria decided to stay in  the wild with her pack and this could be  a hint at Arya's own future but there  are at least two different ways you can  look at this at the end of this story  arya may decide to stay with her own  pack she may decide to stay with her  family instead of running back out into  the wild or arya may decide to go back  into the woods herself arya may never  feel right at home in Winterfell and  after the fighting is done  Arya could leave once again and travel  the world  aurilla did already show interest in  seeing what's west of Westeros so  perhaps that's where she could decide to  go next at the beginning of the series  we did learn how Arya intended on living  her life she said she never wanted to  become a lady she said she didn't want  to ever settle down and have any kids of  her own and she very well may still feel  that way but maybe she doesn't  aurilla story-arc began with her feeling  this way but it doesn't necessarily mean  her story arc will end that way either  typically story arcs end differently  than how they started Arya has spent  most of her life on the run and having  to defend for herself she has seen a lot  of death at a very young age and she was  even responsible for some of those  people dying so when this story ends she  may finally see the light and decide she  is done with that life if her character  is going to ever evolve then she can't  keep living that kind of lifestyle but  is it already too late for Orion to  change her ways now can you teach an old  dog new tricks I would like to think  that you can and most of you that know  me know that I believe horrea may change  her tune once she sees Gendry again Arya  and Gansey had a very special bond but  that was ripped away from her when  Melisandre took Gendry away and as far  as Arya knows she thinks Gendry was  being taken away to die Arya has no idea  Gendry is still alive and when they meet  again in season 8 she is going to be  shocked I think it would be kind of  interesting if arias story ended on a  happier note I think she deserves to  take a break from all the running and  killing her story began with her not  a family but it may end with her  realizing that family is more important  than running off again to King's Landing  to finish her list and the same could  actually be said for Sansa her story  began with her wanting to be a lady and  ultimately becoming the queen but her  story may end with her wanting to be  alone Sansa has learned firsthand just  how ugly forced marriages can be and in  the end  Sansa may decide it would be best if she  stayed single I think that could be a  cool twist on both of these characters  if songs that ended up being the single  one and Arya was the one who settled  down and had a family I don't know how  likely that is to happen but in my heart  of hearts that is what I would like to  see but I think most of you already know  that keep in mind all of this is  assuming Arya survives this series which  is not a guarantee at this point most  people probably don't see Arya ever  settling down though  that doesn't seem to be in her character  and at the 